{
  "$comment": [
    "The Microsoft CoE baseline as changes to Balanced (document 21, section 6.4). Microsoft's words are quoted from the Learn pages checked 2026-11-22 (S2 agent risk tiers, T1 roles and responsibilities). The build applies these operations to Balanced's source rows before wildcards expand.",
    "Rows Balanced already has and this preset keeps: a business owner named at Accept for every tier (accept-business-owner); the autonomy level agreed before go-live for every agent (go-live-autonomy-agent, which covers tier 3); AI holds only supports on intake (intake-s), so a recommendation is an initial assessment, not approval; the business owner alone authorizes a tier 1 change (change-auth-owner, change-auth-a); the security review before tier 3 go-live (go-live-security-tier-3); and the agent risk tier vocabulary mappings.",
    "New seed rows (document 21, section 13.5): role coe-lead, owner roles domain-validator and product-owner, five document types, four review types and the vocabulary list value agent-coe-role.",
    "Chosen here, because document 21 does not name them: coe-lead belongs to the IT party; producesDecisionTypeKey and defaultOwnerRoleKey of the four new review types (release and quality reviews record an acceptance, the maturity review a portfolio decision, the responsible AI assessment a risk acceptance, as the security review does); and reminder days for the two new cadences, following Balanced's cadences at the same tier.",
    "The quality review has a cadence only at tier 2 and the maturity review only at tier 3, as document 21 says. V29 warns about both, and the build still passes (V29 is a warning).",
    "The new document types are not required by a gate, so currentNeedsPerson stays unset. WORKING DEFAULT (open design question 9): only documents a gate requires need a confirmation card when an AI client marks them current.",
    "An upsert merges fields and cannot clear one. Where a decision right moves from an owner role to a role, or the reverse, the Balanced row is retired and a new key takes its place: go-live-a, risk-acceptance-a and retirement-r.",
    "The decision rights follow Microsoft's RACI. The approval rules stay Balanced's, except the tier 2 go-live group: document 21 does not say whether the security reviewer should also approve go-live and risk acceptance.",
    "Gate policy: tier 1 record in test and production; tiers 2 and 3 flag in test; production tier 2 advise and tier 3 enforce with fail closed, as in Balanced; emergencies flag in production with the emergency rule, as in Balanced. In test every change follows its tier (document 21, section 7.6), so gp-emergency-test-tier-1 keeps tier 1 emergencies at record and breaks the tie between gp-test-tier-1 and gp-emergency-test (V09).",
    "Every gate value is a preset value, not a decision: the change gate (D-03) is still open.",
    "Data taxonomy (D-37; docs/architecture/data-taxonomy.md): like Balanced, plus C11 rows that map the domain levels to the Purview governance domain types (Functional unit, Line of business, Data domain, Regulatory, Project; checked 2026-11-24). A top-level domain is a functional unit and a subdomain a data domain. Data set has no matching type: Purview groups data under a domain as data products, which stay in the catalog (principle 4)."
  ],
  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
